  "details": "TLDR; if an AudioClip on avatar is set to \"Decompress On Load\" which doesn't have \"Load In Background\" enabled (Which at least from my experience is literally how Unity imports AudioClips) - the avatar goes through the build process just fine, but then gives out an error \"Avatar Validation Failed\".\n\nIt's really just annoying and has no place making creators play a guessing game.",
